WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:13.559
After Glen's announcement, Ivy turned back to Ezra.

2
00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.520
"I totally get it now.

3
00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.662
Is Glen really leading today's hike?"

4
00:00:19.943 --> 00:00:20.683
Ezra shrugged.

5
00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:24.986
"Mango can't hike with his injured ankle.

6
00:00:25.787 --> 00:00:27.968
That means Larry is in charge of hikes.

7
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.442
And Larry hates to work.

8
00:00:32.303 --> 00:00:34.945
So he'll probably just let Glen take over."

9
00:00:34.965 --> 00:00:40.691
"Yikes. I guess I did help to create a monster," Ivy said.

10
00:00:40.711 --> 00:00:43.373
"Yep," Ezra said.

11
00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:45.175
"He's a beast."

12
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:52.221
and Willow are waiting for me," Ivy said.

13
00:00:52.241 --> 00:00:55.664
"So—" Tweeet!

14
00:00:55.684 --> 00:00:59.647
Ivy spun around and saw Glen, whistle in mouth, followed by Larry.

15
00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:02.770
"Fall in line, campers!"

16
00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:03.931
Glen shouted.

17
00:01:03.951 --> 00:01:08.014
"Everyone had better keep up with me on this hike to Slippery Rock.

18
00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:09.175
Or else!"

19
00:01:10.676 --> 00:01:11.817
Ivy went over to Glen.

20
00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:16.061
"Didn't you mean to say Larry is leading the hike?

21
00:01:16.921 --> 00:01:18.243
And you're his assistant?"

22
00:01:20.805 --> 00:01:24.548
"No." Glen put his hands on his hips and glared at her.

23
00:01:25.504 --> 00:01:26.565
"I said it right.

24
00:01:27.406 --> 00:01:28.627
I'm in charge of the hike."

25
00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:30.869
Larry nodded.

26
00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.853
"Glen is, like, kind of smart for a little dude.

27
00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:39.297
And he's got, like, a ton of enthusiasm."

28
00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:44.081
"I'm incredibly smart," Glen said.

29
00:01:45.582 --> 00:01:47.644
He marched off with Larry following him.

30
00:01:48.725 --> 00:01:51.708
Ivy watched them go, feeling even worse for Ezra.

31
00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:55.469
Living with Glen these days could not be easy.

32
00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:58.389
And then there was the talent show problem.

33
00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.851
"Maybe I can help you with your act somehow," she said.

34
00:02:03.991 --> 00:02:04.791
Ezra perked up.

35
00:02:04.811 --> 00:02:10.053
"How?" Clara and Willow were starting to look annoyed.

36
00:02:10.073 --> 00:02:15.174
"Ivy, we have to rehearse," Clara called.

37
00:02:15.194 --> 00:02:16.974
"I'll be right there."

38
00:02:18.295 --> 00:02:19.335
Ivy looked at Ezra.

39
00:02:19.355 --> 00:02:21.156
"Let me think about it.

40
00:02:21.876 --> 00:02:24.726
I have to go, but I'm sure a good idea will come to me."

41
00:02:25.846 --> 00:02:28.208
Ezra just nodded and stared at the ground.

42
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.611
The girls rehearsed all morning.

43
00:02:33.132 --> 00:02:34.794
Ivy was getting better at dancing.

44
00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:39.017
Or so she thought—until she stepped on Willow's foot.

45
00:02:39.938 --> 00:02:41.699
Again. And again.

46
00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:47.504
When the bugle blew for lunch, Ivy wiped her forehead.

47
00:02:47.524 --> 00:02:50.446
"Whew, I'm ready for a break!"

48
00:02:51.507 --> 00:02:52.268
Willow groaned.

49
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.842
"Yeah, so are my feet."

50
00:02:57.604 --> 00:02:59.105
The girls headed to the mess hall.

51
00:03:00.426 --> 00:03:02.588
They saw Ezra sitting alone at a table.

52
00:03:02.608 --> 00:03:06.872
"I wonder where Glen is," Clara said.

53
00:03:06.892 --> 00:03:09.494
"Ezra and Glen are always together."

54
00:03:09.514 --> 00:03:13.517
"Glen's probably still hiking," Ivy said.

55
00:03:13.537 --> 00:03:15.319
"I'll go sit with Ezra.

56
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.420
He looks lonely."

57
00:03:19.002 --> 00:03:21.344
Ivy got her food and sat across from Ezra.

58
00:03:22.432 --> 00:03:25.235
"Did you think of anything yet for my talent show act?"

59
00:03:25.575 --> 00:03:26.095
he asked.

60
00:03:26.876 --> 00:03:28.317
"I'm running out of time."

61
00:03:28.337 --> 00:03:31.040
"No," Ivy said.

62
00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.424
"Sorry, I've been really busy rehearsing for our act."

63
00:03:35.444 --> 00:03:40.308
"Oh." Ezra had a long drink of bug juice.

64
00:03:40.328 --> 00:03:45.332
"Must be nice to have an act—and people to do it with."

65
00:03:46.814 --> 00:03:49.056
Just then Richard and Annie sat down.

66
00:03:51.104 --> 00:03:54.866
"You two are lucky you didn't go on the Slippery Rock hike," Richard said.

67
00:03:54.886 --> 00:03:57.387
"Why?" Ivy asked.

68
00:03:57.407 --> 00:04:01.468
"Glen was so annoying," Annie said.

69
00:04:01.488 --> 00:04:05.090
"He kept blowing his whistle and yelling at us to keep up."

70
00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.211
"And he kept mixing up facts about wildlife.

71
00:04:10.392 --> 00:04:14.834
Plus, we had to march behind him like we were in the army," Richard said.

72
00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:18.575
"But you'll never guess what happened to him."

73
00:04:18.595 --> 00:04:23.618
"What?" Ivy leaned forward and Ezra looked up.

74
00:04:25.479 --> 00:04:26.760
Richard started laughing.

75
00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:32.324
"There was something moving in a bush, and Glen told us all to stand back.

76
00:04:32.964 --> 00:04:36.587
He said it was a dangerous animal that only he could handle.

77
00:04:37.187 --> 00:04:40.509
He shook the bush Annie grinned.

78
00:04:40.529 --> 00:04:43.091
"And a skunk ran out.

79
00:04:44.332 --> 00:04:45.473
It sprayed Glen!"

80
00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.175
Richard pinched his nose shut.

81
00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:51.355
"It smelled awful!"
